<section class="home-top">
  <h1 class="home-title">See how computers actually work.</h1>
  <p class="home-sub">Three real systems you can poke at: a Huffman compressor that builds its tree in front of you, a key-value store that writes to disk, and a packet network where you can cut a cable and watch the routes heal.</p>
</section>

<section class="modules" aria-label="Modules">
  <a class="module" href="/compression">
    <img src="/img/compression.png" alt="The Huffman tree being built merge by merge" loading="lazy">
    <div class="module-body">
      <span class="module-kicker">Compression</span>
      <h2>Huffman coding</h2>
      <p>Type any text and watch the tree get built one merge at a time, then see every character's code and how many bits you saved.</p>
      <ul><li>Greedy algorithms</li><li>Priority queues</li><li>Prefix codes</li></ul>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a class="module" href="/database">
    <img src="/img/database.png" alt="The key-value store terminal and stored records" loading="lazy">
    <div class="module-body">
      <span class="module-kicker">Storage</span>
      <h2>Key-value store</h2>
      <p>Drive a real store from a terminal with PUT, GET, DELETE and SCAN. Every write lands in a JSON file on disk.</p>
      <ul><li>Hash indexes</li><li>Persistence</li><li>Range scans</li></ul>
    </div>
  </a>
  <a class="module" href="/network">
    <img src="/img/network.png" alt="A mesh network with a packet in flight" loading="lazy">
    <div class="module-body">
      <span class="module-kicker">Networking</span>
      <h2>Packet network</h2>
      <p>Route packets with Dijkstra, cut a cable mid-run and watch them re-route, turn up packet loss and count what gets through.</p>
      <ul><li>Shortest paths</li><li>TTL</li><li>Packet loss</li></ul>
    </div>
  </a>
</section>
